Subject: use the guest path chroot was given, not an uninitialized buffer

OpenSSH's privilege separation (sshd) calls chroot("/var/empty") as fake
root. Even with patch 0016 PRoot then aborted on optimized builds:

    path.c:546: compare_paths2: Assertion `length1 > 0' failed.

handle_chroot_exit_end() reads the guest path into `path_guest` only in the
SIGSYS flow. In the normal flow it read it into `path` (reused for other
things), and later compared the still uninitialized `path_guest` with every
non-root binding of the container (any -b or volume: the compare is skipped
when the only binding is the root one). The buffer is stack garbage; when it
happened to be empty compare_paths() asserted. It only showed with
inlining, which is why a debug build worked.

The guest path now goes into path_guest in both flows, and an unresolvable
chroot target (realpath failed, whose result was ignored) returns its error
instead of being compared as an empty string.

Upstream: termux/proot @ 7266fb3e8516535682f5a9c8f3a7e70f6506eddb (v5.1.107.92), after patches 0001-0016

diff --git a/src/extension/fake_id0/chroot.c b/src/extension/fake_id0/chroot.c
index 2b065cf..657f8b6 100644
--- a/src/extension/fake_id0/chroot.c
+++ b/src/extension/fake_id0/chroot.c
@@ -51,7 +51,10 @@ int handle_chroot_exit_end(Tracee *tracee, Config *config, bool from_sigsys) {
 	if (status < 0)
 		return status;
 
-	realpath(path, path_host_absolute);
+	/* An unresolvable target must not reach compare_paths() with an
+	 * uninitialized buffer (its empty-path assertion aborted PRoot).  */
+	if (realpath(path, path_host_absolute) == NULL)
+		return -errno;
 
 	/* Handle "new rootfs == current rootfs" case.  */
 	status = compare_paths(get_root(tracee), path_host_absolute);
@@ -73,9 +76,9 @@ int handle_chroot_exit_end(Tracee *tracee, Config *config, bool from_sigsys) {
 	/* Fetch guest path if we didn't already.  */
 	if (!from_sigsys) {
 		input = peek_reg(tracee, ORIGINAL, SYSARG_1);
-		status = read_path(tracee, path, input);
+		status = read_path(tracee, path_guest, input);
 		if (status < 0)
-			return -errno;
+			return status;
 	}
 
